<!--
The smallest beet entry: a script that runs on load and prints, the
`node main.js` shape. `<script>` is a raw-text element so the JavaScript body is
verbatim; `ExchangeScriptElement` installs the entry's `Request -> Response`
action (it runs the script and returns its `console.log` as the response), and
`CallOnReady` calls that action once the entry is built, streaming the output to
stdout, then exiting.
-->
<script {(ExchangeScriptElement, CallOnReady)}>console.log("hello world")</script>
